      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Normally you don’t need EMI protection for the debug interface, the SWD/JTAG lines have system voltage level, and are short.<br/>The debug adapter works at the same voltage level (3.3V), so interferences are very unlikely.</p><p>If you have a very EMI-prone environment like motor control or another kind of driver for large inductivities, I would recommend an isolated debug interface.</p><p>As far as I understand it (I am not a hardware guy), these isolated debug adapters are intended to protect the debug adapter and the host, not the target.<br/> </p></div>"
    }
